Running nethack pl10 on a SparcStation running SunOS 4.0.3c, if that matters,
I was inside a shop recently and noticed two things which might be bugs,
or might be coincidences.

I've got my pet with me, got 4 tripe rations too, thinking "No
problem -- this shop is mine."  Well, I was unable to train my pet.
More precisely, he seemed trained to bring me stuff, all right, but he
piled the loot in the wrong spot.

    -----------#     P == Me, the player.
    |       @ P#     @ == Shopkeeper.
    |        X|      X == Location pet insists on putting stuff.

Ok, I figure my luck is running bad or the damned pet just doesn't like
me.  I waltz into the shop to see what I want badly enough to pay, pick up 
a few items, and the shopkeeper moves to block the door.
 
    -----------#     P == Me, the player.
    |        @-#     @ == Shopkeeper.
    |    P    |

Fine, so far so good, I pick stuff up, pay for it, and want to leave.  But
the shopkeeper won't move.  I rest for a long time, check my pack to verify
I've paid up, etc., but he just won't move.  Very annoying -- I can't
escape from the shop!

So, I think: oh, well, guess this guy's screwed, might as well attack
the shopkeeper; so I walk up and hit him.  He's angry, and hits back.  I
retreat, but he won't follow.  So, I toss arrows and stuff at him 'til he's
dead, grab what I really want, and leave.  Pretty convenient having a stuck
shopkeeper; now if only I could make him get stuck without blocking the
door....

Q1: I never had a pet who was such a trouble to train before.  How did I
    convince him to deliver stuff to the wrong square?
Q2: How did I make the shopkeeper get stuck?  Is this related to Q1?  Is
    it a new feature I just learned about, or a pl10 bug?

Perhaps a bug relating to which the pet and shopkeeper thought were adjacent
squares would explain both symptoms?

